    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d35">

                <pb facs="0075" n="25" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg25"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.51/235</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-10-24T19:00:00+03:31"><hi rendition="#italic">October 24,
                                1917, 7 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 27, 4.40
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1904. Leading Moscow commercial paper gives credence to a rumor of cession of
                    Kamchatka Peninsula to the United States for Rs. 20,000,000,000 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">sic</hi>]. In view of constantly growing rumors that our
                    loans to Russia are applying for Russian territory, which idea is undoubtedly
                    encouraged by German propaganda, would appreciate an official denial for
                    publication.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Francis</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
